Decided: plugin::call takes one total deadline; a Conn wrapper sets the socket timeout to the time left before each read and write
Because: "A total deadline per plugin call (connect + send + full read)."
Rejected: keeping per-read timeouts — a backend trickling one byte a second resets them forever
Decided: at most 8 calls in flight per backend URL, the 9th fails at once with "busy"
Because: "a call over the limit fails fast with a clear error instead of queueing on the shared pool"
Rejected: tokio Semaphore — calls run on blocking threads; a counter map with a drop guard is enough and adds no API
Decided: an event stream drops its deadline and gives its place back once streaming starts
Because: crates/cooee-server/src/lib.rs:1379 streams run on their own std thread, not the blocking pool
Decided: the e2e test retries connections the kernel resets (macOS listen queue is 128) but never a read timeout
Check: with IN_FLIGHT raised to 10000 the e2e test fails; the unit test hangs on the old per-read timeout
Owner: a hung or slow plugin now fails its own calls quickly and never slows the rest of cooee
